<title>USA: Cox Radio says buys four staions in Alabama.</title>
<headline>Cox Radio says buys four staions in Alabama.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cox Radio Inc said Wednesday it signed definitive agreements to buy four radio stations in Birmingham, Alabama.</p>
<p>The company said it bought WENN-FM and WAGG-AM from Booker T. Washington Broadcasting Services, and WBHJ-FM and WBHK-FM from H&amp;P Radio LLC.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Cox Radio owns, operates or does sales and marketing for 43 stations in 12 markets.</p>
